---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/brevo-vs-mailchimp';
const title = 'Brevo vs Mailchimp for Shopify Email: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = 'Brevo vs Mailchimp for Shopify — campaign continuity versus sales follow-up and transactional workflows, with Shopify connection and migration checks.';

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should a Shopify team keep Mailchimp?",
    "answer": "Keep it on the shortlist when existing campaign production, audience rules and supported Shopify flows meet the store requirements. Demonstrate a catalog campaign and purchase-triggered journey with the actual operator before paying to migrate."
  },
  {
    "question": "When is Brevo a useful alternative?",
    "answer": "Evaluate Brevo when deal follow-up or API/SMTP transactional sending is a real requirement alongside marketing. Confirm the Shopify app, account connection and required sales automation package; a shared brand does not prove shared entitlements."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which has better cart recovery?",
    "answer": "Compare the same cart, permission and purchase-cancellation cases in both accounts. Product rendering and event freshness matter more than a generic platform ranking. No recovery-rate advantage is established here."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I migrate Mailchimp segments to Brevo?",
    "answer": "Export fields, tags, suppression and permission evidence, then rebuild segment logic and waiting journeys explicitly. Assign one sender per flow and test purchase, withdrawal and duplicate-event handling across cutover."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I consider Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "Only add another candidate for a named unmet workflow. Compare its current integration, export, suppression and operating requirements against the same brief; there is no automatic graduation path from either vendor."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does transactional access replace Shopify order notifications?",
    "answer": "No automatic replacement follows from API access. Map each notification to its actual sender, template and event owner, and verify delivery and duplicate prevention before changing the store configuration."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Brevo automatically better for EU stores?",
    "answer": "Review actual processing terms, locations, subprocessors, retention and purpose-specific permission. Company location does not establish compliance or make imported contacts eligible for marketing."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I compare costs at 8,000 contacts?",
    "answer": "Request matched quotes for contacts, monthly and peak sends, required modules, destinations, message segments, carrier fees and support. Include migration and ongoing labor; contact count alone does not decide the invoice."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Brevo vs Mailchimp</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Brevo vs Mailchimp for Shopify email and SMS planning</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Choose around the work your team owns: continuing a familiar Shopify campaign program, or bringing sales follow-up and transactional sending into the evaluation. Neither is a temporary stepping stone by definition. The scenarios below are proposed evaluations, not observed merchant results.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="mt-12 max-w-4xl">
        <TldrBox picks={[
          { label: 'Campaign continuity', tool: 'Mailchimp', reason: 'A useful candidate for an established operator with supported Shopify events and audience rules.' },
          { label: 'Sales follow-up', tool: 'Brevo', reason: 'Deal pipelines can organize corporate-gifting inquiries; validate the required sales automation package.' },
          { label: 'Service messages', tool: 'Brevo', reason: 'API and SMTP transactional sending provide a concrete integration option, with separate ownership checks.' },
        ]} />
      </div>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Start with the actual Shopify connection</h2>
        <p>Mailchimp documents Shopify customer-event syncing for marketing automations and app controls for tags, discounts and SMS subscriber syncing. That makes it a substantive Shopify candidate, rather than merely a familiar newsletter editor. Inspect which audience receives each event and the current flow entitlements. See <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/mailchimp-shopify-syncing/">Shopify syncing</a> and <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/manage-mailchimp-shopify/">app management</a>.</p>
        <p>Brevo's current Shopify connection documentation names the Brevo PushOwl app. Identify whether the store is starting there or migrating an existing Brevo account before designing the workflow. App installation, account linking, sales tools and transactional sending are separate acceptance items; do not assume an old connector guide establishes today's setup. Use the <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879-Brevo-PushOwl-app-for-Shopify-Connect-your-Shopify-store-with-Brevo-PushOwl">current connection guide</a>.</p>
        <h2>Pottery studio: preserve campaign production before moving</h2>
        <p>For a hypothetical $32k/month pottery studio whose owner has used Mailchimp since 2019, compare a new collection campaign, a back-in-stock signup and a welcome path. Have the owner replace product images, exclude buyers of the featured piece and preview sold-out variants. Mailchimp continuity has value if those tasks work reliably with the existing team. Record actual editing and review effort; familiarity alone does not prove faster production.</p>
        <p>Recreate the same campaign and welcome branches in the proposed Brevo setup. Include wholesale interest, an existing customer signing up again and a withdrawn subscriber. A migration needs a concrete improvement that pays for template rebuilding, audience reconciliation and operator training. No studio switch, savings or subsequent platform upgrade was observed.</p>
        <h2>Meal-kit gifting: a deal is different from a newsletter tag</h2>
        <p>For an illustrative 200 corporate-gifting inquiries per quarter, model inquiry, sales call, quote and bulk order. Brevo's <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/16896790383762-Getting-started-with-Deals">deal stages</a> offer a useful way to track this work. Its <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/15445989568402-Available-triggers-actions-and-rules-in-an-automation">automation reference</a> places deal triggers in specific sales packages. Confirm the package before treating a pipeline demonstration as an automated follow-up solution.</p>
        <p>If Mailchimp already handles the consumer newsletter well and another system owns sales, keeping that boundary can also be sensible. Test the handoff: who follows up an unanswered quote, what happens when a bulk order closes, and how is a sales-only contact excluded from promotional email? A click does not supply new channel or purpose permission. Avoid letting a gifted recipient inherit the buyer's marketing eligibility.</p>
        <h2>German outdoor store: service mail and procurement</h2>
        <p>For a hypothetical $41k/month outdoor store, separate marketing from order-service notifications. Brevo supports <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360021196220-What-are-the-differences-between-marketing-transactional-and-automation-emails">transactional API and SMTP sending</a>. Evaluate that option when an application needs it, but trace the actual Shopify notification owner before enabling another sender. Check retries, duplicate order events, language, sender authentication and support escalation. API availability does not establish an automatic replacement for Shopify receipts.</p>
        <p>Review influencer-list provenance, processing terms, subprocessors, data locations, retention and suppression against the store's procurement requirements. Neither EU company location nor a consent field establishes legal clearance. Keep source, wording, time, purpose and withdrawal attached to imported permissions.</p>
        <h2>Cart, post-purchase and winback acceptance cases</h2>
        <p>Use the same illustrative $75 cart, recovery window and offer in both accounts. Include a changed variant, missing image, expired code and purchase during a wait. Trace current inventory, links, purchase and suppression state immediately before dispatch. Replay the checkout event and delay the purchase event: record duplicate prevention and cancellation behavior, rather than assuming a connector cancels waiting messages.</p>
        <p>For post-purchase education, distinguish gift buyers from recipients and suppress conflicting promotions during an open service case. For winback, exclude current subscribers and recent purchasers and test a return to the store while waiting. Use a suitable holdout with uncertainty before treating attributed recoveries as incremental lift. These are proposed tests, with no measured recovery-rate winner.</p>
        <h2>Cost and a controlled cutover</h2>
        <p>Request matched current quotes at 8,000, 11,000 and 20,000 contacts, including projected sends over eighteen months and peak sale traffic. Include sales modules, transactional volume, support, integration, template work and monitoring. There is no supported fixed contact threshold at which either vendor becomes uneconomic.</p>
        <p>Export tags, fields, permission and suppression; rebuild segments and flows disabled. Retain historical reporting. Assign one sender and queue owner per journey, inspect messages already waiting and verify cancellation acknowledgments before replacement activation. Mailchimp's <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/help/connect-shopify/">connection guide</a> advises pausing existing welcome automations before connecting Shopify; include that collision case in the cutover plan. Set timing by verified coverage rather than a universal migration duration.</p>
        <h2>If SMS is in scope</h2>
        <p>Verify actual destinations, sender registration, plan features and message segments separately. Audit live popup, checkout and keyword wording against the promised message types and weekly frequency. Configure applicable quiet hours by recipient destination and test withdrawal while deferred. Assign STOP/HELP processing and ordinary support replies to an operator; email unsubscribe and SMS withdrawal need explicit mapping. Check reply backlog and opt-outs by flow weekly and revisit capture disclosures as automations change.</p>
        <p>Coordinate cart, VIP launch and SKU replenishment offers using current purchase, subscription, gift and support context. A universal twenty-four-hour spacing rule does not replace eligibility checks. Hypothetical contribution: $100 revenue less $45 product and $10 fulfillment leaves $45; a 25% discount leaves $20 before three texts, carrier fees and operating cost. The discount alone does not establish negative margin. Compare incremental orders and full-price repeat quality alongside costs.</p>
        <h2>Choose the boundary you can operate</h2>
        <p>Keep Mailchimp when its Shopify flows and established campaign process satisfy the brief. Evaluate Brevo positively for the documented deal and transactional jobs, with the current Shopify app and package verified. If neither meets a named requirement, compare another candidate, including Sequenzy, against that requirement instead of forcing an extra lifecycle layer or a future migration.</p>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/brevo-vs-omnisend">Brevo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/drip-vs-mailchimp">Drip vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-mailchimp">Sequenzy vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">Email apps for food & beverage</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Brevo vs Mailchimp FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
